# Calendar

The publishing calendar template presents important dates in a structured, browsable form. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/calendar/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Adapt the information structure for existing household calendar entries, maintenance appointments or collection schedules. Prefer a readable agenda when people mainly need the next event. Display the calendar source, local date and time; distinguish all-day events from timed appointments.

## Structure and behaviour

Group events by date using semantic headings or a table with clear headers. If a calendar grid is necessary, provide a list alternative and a keyboard model that does not require tabbing through every empty cell. Keep next/previous-period controls labelled with their date context.

## Home Assistant boundary

The theme does not generate schedules, infer bank holidays or create calendar entries. Example dates are invented and must not be presented as current household appointments. Keep native timezone, recurrence, cancellations and permission handling with the calendar integration.

## Household agenda

Invented appointments show a dated agenda in Europe/London. The timed visit has a GMT offset; the all-day reminder remains a calendar-date event.

